  {
    "sha": "56f26bdaec419f97aa54d9fbca35f46b32afe984",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKDU2ZjI2YmRhZWM0MTlmOTdhYTU0ZDlmYmNhMzVmNDZiMzJhZmU5ODQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T08:31:19Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T08:31:19Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): doosan-dnm states a touch probe's spindle stopped before its first move\n\n#574 made every built-in mill post write its spindle-stop word after a\ntouch probe's tool change and length offset, so a control whose tool\nchange leaves the spindle turning (a same-tool continuation) still brings\nthe probe to the part stopped. doosan-dnm (#614) came after #574: its\nstartPreamble skipped S/M3 for a stated speed of 0 but wrote no M5, and\nprobe_spindle_stop's MILL_POSTS left it out.\n\ndoosan-dnm now writes M5 there, and joins MILL_POSTS, so both of its\ntests cover it.\n\nFixes #1035\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
